WEBVTT

00:00:03.222 --> 00:00:05.663
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Our first caller this evening is Andy.

00:00:06.028 --> 00:00:06.786
Hi, Andy.

00:00:07.199 --> 00:00:09.538
What’s your tip for being positive?

00:00:09.539 --> 00:00:09.982
<v><b>Andy:</b></v> Hello.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.452
Well, I think it’s very important to live in the present and not in the past.

00:00:14.844 --> 00:00:19.130
Don’t think about mistakes you made in the past – you can’t change things now.

00:00:19.474 --> 00:00:24.639
The important thing is to think about how you can do things better now and in the future.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:26.580
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Thank you, Andy.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.202
And now we have another caller.

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:33.970
What’s your name, please?

00:00:34.224 --> 00:00:36.955
<v><b>Julie:</b></v> Hi, my name’s Julie.

00:00:37.521 --> 00:00:41.771
My tip is think positive thoughts, not negative ones.

00:00:42.227 --> 00:00:46.480
We all have negative thoughts sometimes, but when we start having them,

00:00:46.481 --> 00:00:50.257
we need to stop and try to change them into positive ones.

00:00:50.811 --> 00:00:58.176
Like, if you have an exam tomorrow and you start thinking, ‘I’m sure I’ll fail,’ then you’ll fail the exam.

00:00:58.742 --> 00:01:03.030
So you need to change that negative thought to a positive thought.

00:01:03.805 --> 00:01:07.359
Just think to yourself, ‘I’ll pass that exam’.

00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:10.315
I do this and it usually works.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.773
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Thank you, Julie.

00:01:15.905 --> 00:01:18.250
And our next caller is Martin.

00:01:18.371 --> 00:01:19.208
Hi, Martin.

00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:20.011
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> Hi.

00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:26.907
Um, my tip is don’t spend a lot of time following the news online or on TV.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.512
It’s always bad news and it just makes you feel depressed.

00:01:31.231 --> 00:01:35.773
Read a book or listen to your favourite music instead, and you won’t feel so bad.

00:01:36.576 --> 00:01:38.388
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Thanks, Martin. Good tip!

00:01:42.152 --> 00:01:44.065
And our next caller is Miriam.

00:01:44.377 --> 00:01:45.018
Miriam?

00:01:45.452 --> 00:01:46.006
<v><b>Miriam:</b></v> Hi.

00:01:46.398 --> 00:01:47.481
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Hi, Miriam.

00:01:47.728 --> 00:01:48.822
What’s your tip?

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:53.446
<v><b>Miriam:</b></v> Every week, make a list of all the good things that happened to you,

00:01:53.535 --> 00:01:55.715
on your phone or on a piece of paper.

00:01:56.307 --> 00:02:01.864
Then if you’re feeling a bit sad or depressed, read the list and it’ll make you feel better.

00:02:02.431 --> 00:02:03.552
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Thanks, Miriam.

00:02:07.328 --> 00:02:09.751
And our last call is from Michael.

00:02:09.978 --> 00:02:11.018
Hi, Michael.

00:02:11.044 --> 00:02:11.842
We’re listening.

00:02:12.212 --> 00:02:17.467
<v><b>Michael:</b></v> Hi. I think it’s good to try to use positive language when you speak to other people.

00:02:17.948 --> 00:02:23.413
You know, if your friend has a problem, don’t say, ‘I’m sorry’ or ‘Oh, poor you.’

00:02:23.662 --> 00:02:27.822
Say something positive, like ‘Don’t worry! Everything’ll be OK.’

00:02:28.388 --> 00:02:32.198
That way, you’ll make the other person think more positively about their problem.

00:02:32.753 --> 00:02:33.717
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> Thank you, Michael.

00:02:34.321 --> 00:02:36.409
Well, that’s all we’ve got time for.

00:02:36.588 --> 00:02:39.122
A big thank you to all our callers.